@startuml fig-08-patient-actor-usecase
' =====================================================================
' Figure 8. The patient is the primary actor of every safeguard
' Type            : PlantUML-type, use case diagram
' Paper section   : § 3, The Documented Patient Concerns
' Concern answered: Gemini family 1 (loss of the human element and surgeon
'                   control) and ChatGPT concern 14 (loss of personal care and
'                   surgeon-patient trust). Every safeguard in the parent
'                   protocol is written with the sponsor as the actor: the
'                   sponsor verifies, the sponsor reports, the sponsor halts.
'                   Redrawn as a use case diagram with the patient as the
'                   primary actor, the same safeguards read as capabilities the
'                   patient holds, which is what a use case diagram is for.
' Why this type   : A use case diagram is the only formal notation whose whole
'                   premise is "who can do what". Reassigning the primary actor
'                   is therefore not a cosmetic change; it changes what the
'                   diagram asserts.
'
' TikZ: draw with the uml* vocabulary of patientstyle.sty.
' TikZ: \umlactor for the four human actors; umlusecase ellipses, text width
' TikZ:   26mm, for the twelve use cases; umlpkg boundary rectangle titled
' TikZ:   "Phase 1 PDAC Physical AI trial" fitted over the use cases only.
' TikZ: Patient actor at (-6.4,-4.2), left of the boundary. Surgeon at
' TikZ:   (9.2,-1.6), DSMB at (9.2,-4.6), Sponsor-Investigator at (9.2,-7.6),
' TikZ:   all right of the boundary, so no secondary actor sits on the
' TikZ:   patient's side.
' TikZ: Use cases in three columns at x = -2.2, 1.6, 5.4 and four rows at
' TikZ:   y = -0.8, -3.2, -5.6, -8.0; 2.4 cm row pitch and 3.8 cm column pitch
' TikZ:   leave at least 8 mm of clear space between ellipse edges.
' TikZ: Associations are umlassoc plain lines; <<include>> and <<extend>> are
' TikZ:   umldash with the stereotype set in a white-filled mmlabel node at the
' TikZ:   midpoint so no label sits on a line.
' TikZ: The two long associations from the Patient to the far column route with
' TikZ:   to[out=0,in=180,looseness=0.85] so they pass between rows rather than
' TikZ:   through an ellipse.
' =====================================================================

!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #6C757D
skinparam ActorBorderColor #00417A
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActorFontColor #111111
skinparam UsecaseBorderColor #00417A
skinparam UsecaseBackgroundColor #DCE8F1
skinparam UsecaseFontColor #111111
skinparam RectangleBorderColor #6C757D
skinparam RectangleBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E9ECEF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #6C757D

left to right direction

actor "Participant\n(primary actor)" as PT #DCE8F1
actor "Operating surgeon" as SG
actor "DSMB" as DS
actor "Sponsor-Investigator" as SI

rectangle "Phase 1 PDAC Physical AI trial" as SYS {
  usecase "Consent, or decline\nwith no consequence" as U1 #00417A
  usecase "Opt out of the\nPhysical AI component" as U2 #00417A
  usecase "Set the autonomy level\naccepted per operative step" as U3 #00417A
  usecase "Inspect the Phase 0\nsimulation result" as U4
  usecase "Require a named human\nto approve every motion" as U5 #00417A
  usecase "Trigger a stop\nthrough the surgeon" as U6
  usecase "Accept or decline the\ndaraxonrasib restart" as U7 #00417A
  usecase "Read my own\naudit trail" as U8
  usecase "Withdraw at any visit,\nno reason required" as U9 #00417A
  usecase "Choose the fate of\nbanked specimens" as U10
  usecase "Be told when the software\nversion changes" as U11
  usecase "Receive my day-30 and\nday-90 results directly" as U12
}

PT --> U1
PT --> U2
PT --> U3
PT --> U4
PT --> U5
PT --> U7
PT --> U9
PT --> U10
PT --> U11
PT --> U12

U6 <|-- U5 : <<extend>>\nstop is the\nlimiting case
U8 ..> U4 : <<include>>
U11 ..> U1 : <<include>>\nforces re-consent

SG --> U5
SG --> U6
DS --> U6
SI --> U11
SI --> U12

note bottom of SYS
  Ten of the twelve capabilities are exercised by the participant.
  The two that are not, stopping the device and issuing a version
  notice, are the two that require someone in the room or in the
  build system. Neither can be exercised against the participant.
end note

note right of PT
  In the parent protocol these twelve appear as
  sponsor obligations. Nothing in the protocol
  changed here. Only the actor did.
end note

@enduml
